# {{ .name }} — team template registry

A shared [guppy](https://github.com/nicedata-work/guppy) template
registry owned by your team: templates live in this repo, CI validates
them and builds the registry, and consumers point guppy here once.

## How it works

- `templates/<id>/` — one directory per template (`guppy.toml`,
  `tests.toml`, `testdata/snapshot/`, `template/` payload)
- CI (`.github/workflows/registry.yml`) runs `guppy lint` + `guppy test`
  on every PR, then rebuilds `index.json` + `tarballs/` on merge —
  this repo's checkout is always a complete, current registry

## Team workflow

1. Drop a template into `templates/<id>/` — see the
   [authoring guide](https://github.com/nicedata-work/guppy/blob/main/docs/guides/authoring-templates.md).
2. Open a PR; CI validates it.
3. Merge; CI commits the rebuilt registry.
4. Consumers configure guppy once (per machine):

```toml
# ~/.config/guppy/guppy.toml
[[template.registries]]
name = "team"
git = "<this repo's git URL>"
# ref = "main"
# trust = "full"   # optional: skip the install-time review gate — this org vouches for the registry
```

Then everything resolves from here:

```sh
guppy template search             # team templates (labeled "team") + public ones
guppy new --template <id> mydir   # scaffold from a team template
guppy template update <id>        # move to a newer published version
```

## Local commands

```sh
guppy project build   # rebuild index.json + tarballs/ (scripts/build-registry.py)
guppy project test    # guppy lint + guppy test on every template
guppy project lint    # drift check: fails when the registry is stale
```

Wire direnv for the `gp` shorthand — see
[working on projects](https://github.com/nicedata-work/guppy/blob/main/docs/guides/gp-workflows.md).
